==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Finno-Ugric|eðe|lang=fi}}; a cognate of Hungarian {{term|elõ}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈe̞si]}}
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:Finnish:-esi|-esi]]
*Hyphenation: e·si

===Prefix===
{{fi-pref}}

# [[pre-]], [[fore-]].

====Inflection====
{{fi-decl-pron|1s=[[esi-]]|3s=([[että]])|5s=[[edessä]]|6s=[[edestä]]|7s=[[eteen]]|8s=[[edellä]]|9s=[[edeltä]]|10s=[[edelle]]|13s=[[etenkin]]<br/>[[etenkään]]|7p=[[esiin]]|8p=[[esillä]]|9p=[[esiltä]]|10p=[[esille]]|a4s=([[edes]])|a10s=[[editse]]}}
The cases of {{term|esi-|lang=fi}} serve in Finnish only as adverbs. The instructive singular is always used with the enclitic particle {{term|-kin}} or {{term|-kään}}.

====Antonyms====
*(''pre-, fore-'') [[jälki-]]

====Derived terms====
*adjectives: [[edellinen]], [[etevä]]
*nouns: [[esine]], [[eteinen]]
*verbs: [[edeltää]], [[edetä]], [[edistää]], [[esiintyä]], [[esittää]]

